1
00:00:00,800 --> 00:00:04,629
Welcome to Melody and
Barnaby's Music Nuggets!

2
00:00:05,629 --> 00:00:10,713
Today we are going to learn
about next-door notes.

3
00:00:12,713 --> 00:00:16,171
A piano has white keys.

4
00:00:16,471 --> 00:00:19,232
And black keys.

5
00:00:21,832 --> 00:00:26,219
The very next key…
is called a semitone.

6
00:00:36,019 --> 00:00:39,244
Two semitones… make a tone.

7
00:00:47,844 --> 00:00:48,819
E

8
00:00:48,869 --> 00:00:50,016
F

9
00:00:50,066 --> 00:00:54,499
No key in between… so
it is a semitone too.

10
00:00:59,899 --> 00:01:00,999
B

11
00:01:01,049 --> 00:01:02,149
C

12
00:01:02,199 --> 00:01:03,428
Same here!

13
00:01:08,628 --> 00:01:11,390
Your turn! Listen and look.

14
00:01:11,790 --> 00:01:14,690
Semitone… or tone?

15
00:01:18,590 --> 00:01:19,819
A tone.

16
00:01:22,619 --> 00:01:25,520
Semitone… or tone?

17
00:01:29,420 --> 00:01:31,020
A semitone.

18
00:01:31,920 --> 00:01:33,242
You've got it!

19
00:01:34,942 --> 00:01:36,403
Now it's your turn!

20
00:01:36,603 --> 00:01:40,804
Play Semitone or Tone
and hear the difference!

21
00:01:42,604 --> 00:01:46,914
Grown-ups, subscribe so
you never miss a Nugget.

22
00:01:46,964 --> 00:01:50,148
New ones every Wednesday and Saturday.

23
00:01:50,448 --> 00:01:52,838
See you for the next Nugget!

